# Underrealm Lich: "Pay 4 life: This creature gains indestructible until end of turn. Tap it." The tap is the ability's
# effect, not its cost, so "you can activate Underrealm Lich's last ability even if it's already tapped. It can't be tapped
# again, but it still gains indestructible" (its ruling; CR 702.12b, 701.26a). As Bot2 casts Black Lotus, Bot1 activates it
# twice, the second time with the Lich tapped by the first: 8 life paid. Bot2's Wrath of God then destroys every creature but
# the indestructible Lich, which stays, tapped.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Underrealm Lich
Plains
Plains
Plains x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Black Lotus
Wrath of God
Swamp x4
Swamp x20

